{"kind":"stack","id":"sep-mix-1","title":"Separating mixtures: filtering, sieving and evaporating","theme":{"background":"#fdf6e3","foreground":"#073642","font":"Georgia, serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Mixture"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"Two or more substances mixed together, where each keeps its own properties and can be separated again."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-q","content":"Which method would separate sand from water?"},{"type":"button","id":"c2-a","label":"Filtering","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Melting","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-c","label":"Dissolving","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Which method separates small stones from sand?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"Sieving","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"Evaporating","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Boiling the sand","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"image","picto":"river"},{"type":"text","id":"c4-t","content":"Your class has a cup of salty water with sand in it. How do you start?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Filter the sand out first","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Leave it in the sun to evaporate","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"You filter out the sand. The water is clear, and the salt is still dissolved in it. Next, you let the water evaporate to get the salt back."},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"The sun slowly evaporates the water, but the sand is still there. You have to filter the sand out afterwards."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-q","content":"When water evaporates, what is left behind?"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-a","label":"The salt","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Nothing at all","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-c","label":"More water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"Evaporation"},{"type":"text","id":"c8-e","content":"When a liquid is heated or left in the air, it turns into a gas and leaves the solid behind."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Which mixture could you separate by sieving?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"Pebbles and sand","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Salt and water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"Milk and cream","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which change of state happens when water evaporates?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"Liquid to gas","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Liquid to solid","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Gas to solid","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"Well done! You finished the separating mixtures lesson."},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"You now know how filtering, sieving and evaporating can separate the parts of a mixture."}],"actions":[]}}
